{
  "format": "attome-audit-hash-v2-test-vector/1",
  "spec": "document/decisions/security/D-539.md (ruling 3); if this file and that text disagree, the text wins and this file is regenerated",
  "notes": [
    "Every field is u16 field_no (big-endian), a presence tag u8 (0x00 NULL/absent, 0x01 present), then when present LP(value) = u32 big-endian byte length followed by the bytes.",
    "The stream starts with LP(\"ATTOME-AUDIT-EVENT\") || u16(2). Header fields 1-29 follow in order, then field 40 (details), 41 (snapshot), 42 (attachments).",
    "Field 40 and field 42 are present (0x01) with value = u32 count followed by LP(row bytes) per row; rows use the same field syntax. Details are ordered by field_name bytes; attachments by document_ref bytes then content_sha256 bytes.",
    "Field 41 is 0x00 with no snapshot row, else 0x01 then LP(row bytes) with fields 1 version (i64), 2 trigger (i32), 3 snapshot canonical text.",
    "Integers are two's-complement big-endian inside their LP; uuid is its 16 RFC 9562 bytes; bool is one byte; timestamptz is i64 microseconds since the Unix epoch (UTC); content_sha256 is its 32 raw bytes.",
    "event.snapshots[].snapshot_json is the stored jsonb value: a JSON string encodes as its UTF-8 content, anything else as its RFC 8785 serialization.",
    "content_digest = lowercase hex SHA-256(canonical bytes). event_hash = lowercase hex SHA-256(\"ATTOME-AUDIT-CHAIN\" || 0x00 || u16(2) || LP(prev_hash ASCII) || content_digest raw 32 bytes).",
    "v1_prev inputs hash with the v1 formula: SHA-256(prev_hash || operation i32 LE || entity_name bytes if present || record_id 16 bytes if present || user_id 16 bytes || changed_on_millis i64 LE)."
  ],
